      "side": 1,
      "message": "This actually had to be reverted back to maven shade plugin.\n\nThe metaInf-services handler in maven-assembly-plugin does not correctly merge META-INF/services files across many separate dependency jars. For org.opendaylight.yangtools.binding.meta.YangModelBindingProvider — which is registered separately by dozens of YANG-model jars (each generated YANG module gets its own registration) — the assembly-plugin build kept only 1 line (ietf-yang-types), silently dropping   \n  every other registration, including iana-if-type. That\u0027s why ServiceLoader.load(YangModelBindingProvider.class) found nothing matching iana-if-type in schemaServiceConfig, producing the empty Set\u003cYangModuleInfo\u003e and the \"Provided list of YangModuleInfo is empty\" exception.\n\norg.opendaylight.gnmi.simulatordevice.utils.EffectiveModelContextBuilder$EffectiveModelContextBuilderException: Provided list of YangModuleInfo  is empty                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n          at org.opendaylight.gnmi.simulatordevice.utils.EffectiveModelContextBuilder.addYangModulesInfo(EffectiveModelContextBuilder.java:67)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               \n          at org.opendaylight.gnmi.simulatordevice.impl.SimulatedGnmiDevice.start(SimulatedGnmiDevice.java:128)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              \n          at org.opendaylight.gnmi.simulatordevice.main.GnmiSimulatorApp.start(GnmiSimulatorApp.java:50)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     \n          at org.opendaylight.gnmi.simulatordevice.main.GnmiSimulatorApp.main(GnmiSimulatorApp.java:29)",
